You are a Senior Performance Engineer and Full-Stack Architect.

Design and implement a production-grade Performance Testing Platform built around Apache JMeter.

The system should be modular, scalable, cloud-ready, and enterprise-grade.

-----------------------------------
🎯 OBJECTIVE
-----------------------------------
Build a web-based application that allows users to:
- Create, manage, and execute performance tests using JMeter
- Monitor real-time metrics
- Analyze historical performance trends
- Integrate with CI/CD pipelines
- Run distributed load tests

-----------------------------------
🏗️ ARCHITECTURE
-----------------------------------
Use a microservices-based architecture:

Frontend:
- React (with TypeScript)
- Dashboard with real-time charts (use WebSockets)

Backend:
- Node.js (Express) OR Python (FastAPI)
- REST + WebSocket APIs

Execution Engine:
- Apache JMeter (CLI mode)
- Wrapper service to trigger and manage JMeter test plans (.jmx)

Database:
- PostgreSQL (test configs, results metadata)
- Redis (real-time metrics streaming / caching)

Storage:
- S3-compatible storage (for logs, reports)

-----------------------------------
⚙️ CORE FEATURES
-----------------------------------

1. Test Plan Management
- Upload, edit, version control JMeter .jmx files
- Parameterization support (CSV, env variables)
- Template library for common scenarios (API, UI, DB)

2. Test Execution
- Run tests on-demand or scheduled
- Support local + distributed execution
- Configure:
  - Threads (users)
  - Ramp-up
  - Duration
  - Loop count

3. Distributed Load Testing
- Master-slave JMeter architecture
- Auto-scale load generators using Docker/Kubernetes
- Ability to add/remove nodes dynamically

4. Real-time Monitoring
- Live metrics:
  - Throughput
  - Response time (avg, p95, p99)
  - Error rate
- WebSocket streaming
- Grafana-compatible metrics

5. Reporting & Analysis
- Generate HTML reports from JMeter
- Trend analysis across multiple runs
- SLA validation (pass/fail rules)
- Comparison between builds

6. CI/CD Integration
- Provide REST API + CLI tool
- Jenkins/GitHub Actions integration
- Fail pipeline if SLA breaches

7. Alerting & Notifications
- Email / Slack alerts
- Trigger alerts on:
  - High error rate
  - SLA breach
  - Test completion

8. User Management & RBAC
- Roles: Admin, Tester, Viewer
- Authentication (JWT / OAuth)

9. Logs & Debugging
- Centralized logs (ELK stack optional)
- Ability to download JMeter logs
- Failure root cause insights

10. Test Data Management
- CSV data upload
- Dynamic data generation
- Secrets management (API keys, tokens)

